WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — agency (90s) Narrator Joy

1
00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:05.694
Modern AI leaderboards count tokens per second or raw score,

2
00:00:05.694 --> 00:00:10.461
ignoring whether the machine burned a kilowatt or a milliwatt.

3
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:20.584
Thermodynamic Bounds for Goal-Holding Agents derives exact rate limits linking bit erasure,

4
00:00:20.584 --> 00:00:23.643
channel capacity, and action cadence.

5
00:00:26.241 --> 00:00:29.889
On this three-dimensional tempo manifold,

6
00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:40.033
static idle draw punishes hesitation while superlinear dissipation punishes panic, carving a golden optimal ridge.

7
00:00:42.631 --> 00:00:45.646
Unfinished or wrong runs score zero.

8
00:00:45.646 --> 00:00:53.015
Among agents that cross the verification gate, intelligence reads as progress per joule.

9
00:00:55.614 --> 00:01:01.925
Two pre-registered experimental rounds across desktop and Jetson hosts confirm

10
00:01:01.925 --> 00:01:08.318
that adaptive tempo selectors preserve budget without sacrificing task closure.

11
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:17.992
Host counters are explicitly labeled reported_j rather than board-shunt measured_j,

12
00:01:17.992 --> 00:01:22.851
anchoring every physical claim to reproducible artifacts.
